// Turbo Bay, inspired by Speed Bay in Moto Racer: a figure of eight on a
// hilly island, with the sea all around and two bays cutting in towards its
// waist. The first loop goes clockwise and the second anticlockwise, and
// halfway round the road climbs back over the ridge it first went through
// in a tunnel.
//
// 1. The start straight is a seafront promenade heading north: railing,
//    beach and sea on the left; palms and tall, colourful hotels on the
//    right.
// 2. On level into a steep banked right-hander at the water's edge, and the
//    road climbs east into a tunnel through the ridge at the island's waist.
// 3. Out of the tunnel, past an old-style grand hotel on a headland above
//    the south-east bay, to a pass between rocks.
// 4. The east coast road rises and falls behind a white barrier, with the
//    sea on the right.
// 5. A mountain road climbs on north in S-bends between rock walls, 37 m
//    up, over a broad top with the lighthouse straight ahead below, and
//    dives steeply at it to the foot of its tower on the northern cape,
//    round a long left-hander.
// 6. Back up through a forest it climbs, eases off over a broad shoulder
//    and rises again, then runs down the ridge and crosses over the tunnel,
//    down the shore of the bay to a bridge with red arches over the river
//    mouth.
// 7. Up a gorge to an arch dam; away from it up the hillside to a hairpin
//    over the east coast, and back down straight onto its crest, narrow,
//    the lake mirroring the hills on the left over a low parapet; down
//    through the town and back to the seafront.
//
// Where things are, in metres from the finish line:
//
// - the seafront:            Span(4304.0, 250.0)
// - the tunnel:              Span(505.0, 625.0)
// - the rock pass:           Span(870.0, 990.0)
// - the east coast:          Span(1000.0, 1280.0)
// - the mountain:            Span(1280.0, 1660.0)
// - the cape, at the foot of
//   the lighthouse:          Span(1560.0, 1700.0)
// - the forest:              Span(1660.0, 2160.0)
// - the bay shore:           Span(2460.0, 2710.0)
// - the red bridge:          Span(2720.0, 2805.0)
// - the gorge:               Span(2830.0, 3100.0)
// - down the hillside at
//   the dam:                 Span(3480.0, 3706.0)
// - the dam's crest:         Span(3706.0, 3858.0), its walls 5.5 m from the
//                            middle, narrow as a dam's
// - the town:                Span(3984.0, 4294.0)
//
// The lighthouse stands on the northern cape at (480.0, -1046.0); the square
// with the monument, by the far end of the crest on the lake's side as at El
// Atazar, at (76.0, 462.0). The lake is at 41 m, a couple of metres under
// the road along the crest, so it shows over the parapet.
//
// How a circuit's file is written: see src/circuits/data.rs. Its mountains
// are a function, in src/circuits/turbo_bay.rs.
(
    name: "Turbo Bay",
    name_en: "Turbo Bay",
    description: "Inspirada en Moto Racer: paseo marítimo, túnel bajo\nla propia pista, puerto de montaña y puente rojo",
    description_en: "Inspired by Moto Racer: seafront, a tunnel under\nthe track itself, a mountain pass and red bridge",
    // A bay: the sea and many gulls, and the wind off it.
    ambience: (
        sea: 0.9,
        gulls: 0.9,
        birds: 0.15,
        cicadas: 0.0,
        wind: 0.35,
    ),
    song: (file: "turbo_bay.mp3", length: 163.1, loudness: -16.0),
    pace: 1.0,
    layout: (
        control_points: [
            // 1. The seafront, north (-Z).
            (0.0, 0.0),
            (0.0, -95.0),
